{"id": "EUVD-2026-76390", "enisaUuid": "d1e1eb61-d35b-30e0-9612-2e3807dafaf2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nlockd: fix NULL dereference on lockowner allocation failure\n\nnlmclnt_locks_init_private() installs NLM file lock operations even when\nnlmclnt_find_lockowner() fails to allocate a lockowner. nlmclnt_proc()\nthen returns -ENOMEM, but the VFS still tears down the partially\ninitialized file_lock and calls locks_release_private().\n\nThat invokes nlmclnt_locks_release_private(), which dereferences\nfl->fl_u.nfs_fl.owner and crashes because the owner was never installed.\n\nClear fl_ops before attempting to initialize the NLM private state, and\ninstall the NLM lock operations only after a lockowner has been allocated\nsuccessfully.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:36", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6db5af172ccc3223c8f730a9a4212f6427feee3e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/07adfbb3de7529f58ca708a97ead7fa4fdb71056", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d662f7fc04fde305a27f304b3cd19b614d366839", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51af080ca4e553256c59a75a877b9b4fff828311", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4c7fc129db061c7daab841c4f3c342d894832362"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7hg8-pf72-7jmh", "CVE-2026-89484"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3a8afa01-9bdb-399e-959c-80da07a82a18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "3d776f60-f8d8-356b-a427-0a4b279cae77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <51af080ca4e553256c59a75a877b9b4fff828311"}, {"id": "4f3a7f69-f093-3cf9-848e-0fb8b37d40b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "687dc29e-d3bf-3c4d-8135-30cbb5dee83c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6ba9bc48-512f-3485-9150-34c5037b563e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <4c7fc129db061c7daab841c4f3c342d894832362"}, {"id": "6f8f605d-fdd2-30c6-8074-af0a5359e74e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <6db5af172ccc3223c8f730a9a4212f6427feee3e"}, {"id": "74f6f428-df6f-346b-9799-057fc8742a54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "7633ad49-3ef9-3ef4-b269-f3a9361f38bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <07adfbb3de7529f58ca708a97ead7fa4fdb71056"}, {"id": "9f7d4578-73bd-3c99-b614-61ce93fc67e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "9f919b24-4624-3ffe-b41e-672df5998dec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "b8a9b3d1-5c5e-38b8-8669-c414f46f8a5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <d662f7fc04fde305a27f304b3cd19b614d366839"}, {"id": "c60736ff-4467-34c3-96bf-d0a1798a1362", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7166c7aa-fe5d-36f0-a7a4-5e7b47584dda", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}